<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Antonio Pérez</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1540">1540</a>–<a href="/years/1611">1611</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Antonio Pérez was secretary of state to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-ii-of-spain">Philip II of Spain</a>. Implicated in the murder of Juan de Escobedo, secretary of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-of-austria">Don John of Austria</a>, in 1578, he was arrested and in 1590 escaped to Aragon, where he claimed the protection of the Justicia. The crown's attempt to move him to the prison of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portuguese-inquisition">Inquisition</a> provoked the riots of 1591 in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zaragoza">Zaragoza</a> and a royal invasion. He fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> and wrote against Philip.</p></div>
